      "severity": "minor",
      "observation": "The range a_m in [0,1] for arbitrary alpha_m, beta_m in [0,1], and the transfer of absolute continuity and singularity between the binary-sequence and real-sequence realizations, are asserted without an argument in the entry. The upper bound follows from the sum-of-squares identity 2(1-a_m) = (sqrt(alpha_m)-sqrt(beta_m))^2 + (sqrt(1-alpha_m)-sqrt(1-beta_m))^2 written at annex lines 239-245 and 290-295, which the definition does not reference. Not judged a coverage gap."
